[agent] ## Summary
[agent] **Deliverable produced:** Feature group `scoresb6c522`, version 1, on the Hopsworks platform — `online_enabled: true`, record key `account_id`, columns exactly `account_id` (string) + `score` (double), **80 rows (one per account)**.
[agent] **How it was done — entirely platform-side:**
[agent] 1. Ingested `data/feature_history.csv` (554 revisions) into a feature group `feathistb6c522` v1 via `hops fg insert`.
[agent] 2. Ran the scoring as a **Hopsworks PYTHON job on the cluster** (`hops job deploy … --run --wait`) — the platform's canonical compute path. The job, on the cluster, reads the history FG, keeps only revisions with `event_time ≤ T = 1773590400000`, takes the most recent revision per account, computes `score = round(sigmoid(w_f1·f1 + w_f2·f2 + w_f3·f3 + bias), 6)`, and writes the result FG with `online_enabled=True`.
[agent] 3. Verified: all 80 accounts have a valid revision at/before T (none excluded); FG metadata confirms online store enabled and correct schema; job logs confirm 80 rows scored and inserted.
[agent] **One interface note (not a blocker):** The `hops sql` / `hops trino` path could not read the offline feature-group table — both the `hudi` and `iceberg` Trino connectors rejected it (`UNSUPPORTED_TABLE_TYPE: "Not a Hudi/Iceberg table"`), so SQL-based scoring wasn't viable. The Job (SDK-on-cluster) path worked cleanly and kept all computation on the platform.
